@startuml sequence_diagram_planning
autonumber
title WEB01 - UC4: execute a forecast and consult its result
hide footbox

actor "LaPrizza Manager" as User
participant "Planning page (WEB07)" as Page
participant "planningApi (WEB07)" as Adapter
participant ModuleRequest as Request
participant apiClient as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Procurement planning API" as Procurement
participant "Backoffice API" as Backoffice

ref over User, Gateway : SD3 - Open planning in the shared shell
User -> Page : Execute a saved forecast
Page -> Page : Generate execution ID and keep the selection
Page --> User : Show progress and disable repeat submission
Page -> Adapter : execute(request with execution ID)
Adapter -> Request : request(POST, execution path, options)
Request -> Client : request with current access bearer
Client -> Gateway : POST selected forecast with execution ID
Gateway -> Procurement : Route planning request
Procurement -> Backoffice : Check current Manager access (AA04)
Backoffice --> Procurement : Actor ID, 401, 403 or failure
alt Authorised
    ref over Procurement, Backoffice : AI01 execution flow\nClaim attempt, load inputs, save outcome atomically
    Procurement --> Gateway : Stored state or diagnostic
else Denied or authority unavailable
    Procurement --> Gateway : Access error or service error
end
alt Response received
    Gateway --> Client : Response
    Client --> Request : Stored state or ApiError
    Request --> Adapter : Stored state or ApiError
    Adapter --> Page : Stored state or ApiError
    Page --> User : Show result or feedback
else Response lost
    Gateway -x Client : Response lost or timed out
    Client --> Request : Unconfirmed request outcome
    Request --> Adapter : Unconfirmed request outcome
    Adapter --> Page : Look up original execution ID
end

opt Recover after a lost response or open a saved result
    Page -> Adapter : getResult(executionId)
    Adapter -> Request : request(GET, result path, options)
    Request -> Client : request with current access bearer
    Client -> Gateway : GET status or result by execution ID
    Gateway -> Procurement : Route result read
    Procurement -> Backoffice : Check current Manager access again (AA04)
    alt Authorised
        Backoffice --> Procurement : Actor ID
        Procurement -> Backoffice : Read execution state (private records API)
        Backoffice --> Procurement : Stored state or lookup diagnostic
        Procurement --> Gateway : Status, result or lookup diagnostic
    else Denied or authority unavailable
        Backoffice --> Procurement : 401, 403 or failure
        Procurement --> Gateway : Access error or service error
    end
    Gateway --> Client : Response
    Client --> Request : Stored state or ApiError
    Request --> Adapter : Stored state or ApiError
    Adapter --> Page : Stored state or ApiError
    Page --> User : Show result, progress or diagnostic
    opt Lookup permits retry and Manager chooses it
        Page -> Adapter : execute(same ID and selection)
        ref over Adapter, Backoffice : Repeat the start flow for the same execution
    end
end
@enduml
